#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_agro_surface_l10n_mx
msgid ""
"==========================\n"
"Mexico - Agro Surface (SIAP)\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Localization bridge between ``agro_base`` and ``l10n_mx_edi_extended``.\n"
"Provides the SIAP planted-surface fact table and the agrochemical\n"
"value-by-zone BI report, mapped to the official Mexican state/municipality\n"
"padrón. Auto-installs when both dependencies are present.\n"
"\n"
"Models\n"
"======\n"
"\n"
"* ``l10n_mx.siap`` -- **flat** planted-surface reference data, one row per\n"
"  ``year × municipality × crop`` (20,223 rows for SIAP 2024). Selected\n"
"  dimensions ``city_id`` (M2o ``res.city``) and ``crop_id`` (M2o ``agro.crop``);\n"
"  ``state_id`` and ``group_id`` are stored related through them. Stores only the\n"
"  source ``planted_area``. Read-only in the UI (filled by the loader).\n"
"  ``UNIQUE(year, city_id, crop_id)``.\n"
"* ``l10n_mx.siap.report`` -- **read-only SQL view** (``_auto = False``) that\n"
"  derives the agrochemical market value (group USD/ha rate × planted area) per\n"
"  category plus ``total_value``, joining ``l10n_mx.siap`` with the crop-group\n"
"  value master. This is the value-by-zone pivot/graph report. No measure is\n"
"  stored and there is no recompute (Odoo report pattern, like ``sale.report``).\n"
"* ``agro.crop.group`` (inherited) -- gains the agrochemical value master: the\n"
"  user enters ``l10n_mx_sales_total`` and ``l10n_mx_hectares_total`` plus the\n"
"  per-category shares (``l10n_mx_*_pct``, read from the master's H/I/F %\n"
"  columns); ``l10n_mx_investment_value`` (= sales / hectares) and each\n"
"  per-category ``l10n_mx_*_value`` (= investment × pct / 100) are **stored\n"
"  computed**. A non-blocking alert at the top of the form flags shares over 100%.\n"
"\n"
"The base models ``agro.crop.group`` and ``agro.crop`` live in ``agro_base``;\n"
"this bridge ships the 37 crop groups (with their value master) and the 139 SIAP\n"
"``Nomcultivo`` crops (one ``agro.crop`` per group × crop) as data.\n"
"\n"
"Menus: **Agronomy > Reporting > Value by Zone & Crop** (pivot/graph, all users)\n"
"and **Agronomy > Configuration > Business Intelligence > SIAP Data** (managers).\n"
"\n"
"Geographic mapping\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"SIAP ``Nomestado`` / ``Nommunicipio`` are resolved by normalized name (lower,\n"
"accent-folded) against ``res.country.state`` (``l10n_mx``) and ``res.city``\n"
"(``l10n_mx_edi_extended`` padrón): 32/32 states and 99.4% of municipalities\n"
"match directly. The remainder is handled as follows:\n"
"\n"
"* **12 municipalities** absent from the padrón (created 2017-2021) are added to\n"
"  ``l10n_mx_edi_extended/data/res.city.csv`` with their official INEGI codes\n"
"  (San Quintín; Seybaplaya, Dzitbalché; six Chiapas municipalities; Coatetelco,\n"
"  Xoxocotla, Hueyapan).\n"
"* **3 Oaxaca names** that differ from the padrón are mapped via\n"
"  ``MUNICIPALITY_CROSSWALK`` (Tezoatlán honorific; the two Mixtepec districts).\n"
"\n"
"The loader is **fail-loud**: any crop or municipality that does not resolve\n"
"aborts the load (before the wipe), listing the unresolved keys.\n"
"\n"
"Data pipeline (data-as-code)\n"
"============================\n"
"\n"
"Source masters live outside the repo (value XLSX + SIAP CSV). They are\n"
"transformed by ``tools/prepare_siap_data.py`` into versioned data files:\n"
"\n"
"* ``data/agro_crop_group_data.xml`` -- 37 crop groups with USD/ha values.\n"
"* ``data/agro_crop_data.xml`` -- one ``agro.crop`` per (group, SIAP Nomcultivo);\n"
"  loaded after the groups so its ``group_id`` refs resolve.\n"
"* ``data/l10n_mx.siap.csv`` -- 20,223 rows, loaded **programmatically** by\n"
"  ``l10n_mx.siap._import_csv`` (idempotent wipe-by-year) from the\n"
"  ``post_init_hook``. Declared under ``oca_data_manual`` so it is not reloaded\n"
"  on every upgrade. The CSV carries **no** ``id`` column and references each\n"
"  crop by ``crop_id:id``.\n"
"\n"
"Regenerate after a source change::\n"
"\n"
"    python tools/prepare_siap_data.py \\\n"
"        --xlsx \"<value master>.xlsx\" \\\n"
"        --csv \"<SIAP surface>.csv\" \\\n"
"        --out-dir data/\n"
"\n"
"The script normalizes group names and applies a small **crosswalk** for names\n"
"that do not match by normalization alone, and **fails explicitly** listing any\n"
"group that does not resolve, so a new source year cannot silently drop rows.\n"
"\n"
"Architecture decision -- flat data vs SQL report\n"
"================================================\n"
"\n"
"The agrochemical USD totals are **not** stored on the flat data. Following the\n"
"Odoo report pattern (``sale.report``, ``account.invoice.report``): the flat\n"
"reference data lives in ``l10n_mx.siap`` (operational/config) and the derived\n"
"measures live in ``l10n_mx.siap.report``, an ``_auto = False`` SQL view that\n"
"computes rate × area on read. This keeps the flat model free of derived\n"
"columns and avoids any recompute over the 20k rows when a value-master rate\n"
"changes.\n"
"\n"
"Depends\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"``agro_base``, ``l10n_mx_edi_extended``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_ledger_maintenance
msgid ""
"==========================\n"
"Product Asset Maintenance\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Preventive and corrective maintenance management for equipment tracked as product assets (lot/serial numbers).\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"Maintenance Plans\n"
"-----------------\n"
"\n"
"A plan is core Maintenance's ``maintenance.plan`` on an asset, extended here:\n"
"\n"
"* **Interval-based scheduling**: every N days, weeks, months or years\n"
"* **Counted from completion**: by default the next request falls one interval after\n"
"  the day the last one came back; a plan can count on fixed dates instead\n"
"* **One open request**: the plan always holds its next request, ahead of time\n"
"* **Distance trigger**: a plan can also fall due by odometer, read off the asset's meter\n"
"* **Archive to pause**: an archived plan opens no request; unarchiving resumes it\n"
"* **Compliance metrics**: completed vs cancelled requests\n"
"* **Conflict detection**: alerts when several plans fall due the same day\n"
"\n"
"Maintenance Plan Templates\n"
"--------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Standardize maintenance across similar equipment:\n"
"\n"
"* **Reusable templates**: Define interval, duration, and instructions once\n"
"* **Mass application**: Apply templates to multiple equipment via wizard\n"
"* **Asset type filtering**: Templates can target specific asset types (vehicle, equipment, machinery)\n"
"\n"
"Maintenance Requests\n"
"--------------------\n"
"\n"
"A request is core Maintenance's ``maintenance.request`` on an asset. The stock\n"
"transfers are only the equipment's trip to the workshop and back:\n"
"\n"
"* **Send to Maintenance**: creates the transfer to the warehouse's maintenance location\n"
"* **Stages follow the transfers**: validating the outgoing transfer puts the request in\n"
"  progress; validating its return closes it\n"
"* **Equipment validation**: the return must bring back the equipment that was sent\n"
"* **Vendor tracking**: the supplier performing external maintenance\n"
"* **Return metrics**: planned end vs actual return, and the delay\n"
"\n"
"Equipment State Tracking\n"
"------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Know where your assets are at any moment:\n"
"\n"
"* **Operational states**:\n"
"\n"
"  - *In Storage*: Available in warehouse\n"
"  - *Deployed*: In operational use at field/site\n"
"  - *In Maintenance*: Under repair\n"
"\n"
"* **Maintenance health**:\n"
"\n"
"  - *Good*: No open request due\n"
"  - *Warning*: A preventive request is due or under way\n"
"  - *Critical*: A corrective request is open\n"
"\n"
"Warehouse Configuration\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"Enable maintenance and deployment per warehouse:\n"
"\n"
"* **Maintenance operations**:\n"
"\n"
"  - Dedicated maintenance location (``WH/Maintenance``)\n"
"  - Maintenance picking type with sequences\n"
"  - Maintenance return picking type\n"
"\n"
"* **Deployment operations**:\n"
"\n"
"  - Dedicated deployed location (``WH/Deployed``)\n"
"  - Deployment picking type\n"
"  - Deployment return picking type\n"
"\n"
"Asset Log Integration\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"Automatic history tracking:\n"
"\n"
"* Creates ``resource.asset.log`` entries when maintenance is completed\n"
"* Records maintenance type, duration, vendor, and timing metrics\n"
"* Links logs to the originating maintenance request\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"1. **Enable maintenance in warehouse**:\n"
"\n"
"   Go to *Inventory > Configuration > Warehouses*, edit your warehouse,\n"
"   and check \"Allow Maintenance\". This creates the maintenance location\n"
"   and picking types automatically.\n"
"\n"
"2. **Enable deployment (optional)**:\n"
"\n"
"   In the same warehouse form, check \"Allow Deployment\" to enable\n"
"   equipment deployment tracking.\n"
"\n"
"3. **Mark products for maintenance**:\n"
"\n"
"   On the product form, enable \"Recurring Maintenance\" under the\n"
"   Maintenance tab. This allows lot/serial numbers of this product\n"
"   to have maintenance plans.\n"
"\n"
"4. **Create maintenance templates**:\n"
"\n"
"   Go to *Maintenance > Configuration > Plan Templates* to create\n"
"   reusable maintenance schedules.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Creating a Maintenance Plan\n"
"---------------------------\n"
"\n"
"1. Open the asset, or *Maintenance > Maintenance Plans*\n"
"2. Select a template or set the interval, how it counts, and the first occurrence\n"
"3. Save: the plan opens its first request on that date\n"
"\n"
"Manual Maintenance Request\n"
"--------------------------\n"
"\n"
"1. From the asset form, click \"Request a Maintenance\"\n"
"2. Fill in the maintenance details (type, duration, vendor)\n"
"3. Click \"Send to Maintenance\" to move the equipment to the maintenance location\n"
"4. When the work is done, return the transfer to bring the equipment back;\n"
"   validating the return closes the request and logs the service\n"
"\n"
"Scheduled Maintenance\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"A daily cron sends out every plan's open order that is due by date or by odometer,\n"
"creating one transfer, carrying every serial of the order, through the assets' warehouse. A second daily cron refreshes the\n"
"plan and asset states that depend on the date.\n"
"\n"
"Dependencies\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"* ``asset_ledger``: Base asset tracking functionality\n"
"* ``maintenance``: the order and the plan, which maintain resources and the assets on them\n"
"\n"
"Technical Notes\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
"* Uses Odoo's native ``return_ids`` field for tracking return pickings\n"
"* Location flags (``maintenance_location``, ``deployed_location``) are mutually exclusive\n"
"* Up to version 19.0.1.11.0 the request was a ``stock.picking``; the 19.0.1.12.0 migration\n"
"  turns each such picking into a ``maintenance.request`` and links the picking and its\n"
"  return to it\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin Development Team\n"
"\n"
"Maintainer\n"
"==========\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by AgroMarin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_invoice_margin_sale
msgid ""
"===========================\n"
"Account Invoice Margin Sale\n"
"===========================\n"
"\n"
"..\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: sha256:4b6cc430e226d789e638616e03761cc6c56aea0be0b262601335bd62ba16d253\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Production%2FStable-green.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Production/Stable\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-OCA%2Fmargin--analysis-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/tree/19.0/account_invoice_margin_sale\n"
"    :alt: OCA/margin-analysis\n"
".. |badge4| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/weblate-Translate%20me-F47D42.png\n"
"    :target: https://translation.odoo-community.org/projects/margin-analysis-19-0/margin-analysis-19-0-account_invoice_margin_sale\n"
"    :alt: Translate me on Weblate\n"
".. |badge5| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/runboat-Try%20me-875A7B.png\n"
"    :target: https://runboat.odoo-community.org/builds?repo=OCA/margin-analysis&target_branch=19.0\n"
"    :alt: Try me on Runboat\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3| |badge4| |badge5|\n"
"\n"
"This module makes an invoice line created from a sale order take its cost\n"
"from that order line instead of from the product, and keeps down payments\n"
"out of the margin an invoice reports.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"This module is autoinstalable.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Once installed, the cost of every invoice line created from a sale order\n"
"is taken from the sale order line instead of from the product, and it\n"
"keeps tracking the sale order after the invoice is posted. Lines that\n"
"come from a down payment are left out of the invoice margin.\n"
"\n"
"Because the invoice line keeps tracking its sale order line, editing the\n"
"cost on the invoice does not stick: the next change to the line or its\n"
"invoice puts the sale order's figure back. Change the cost on the sale\n"
"order line instead.\n"
"\n"
"The cost is converted into the invoice's currency at the invoice date,\n"
"so an order priced in one currency can be invoiced in another and the\n"
"margin still compares two figures in the same currency.\n"
"\n"
"When an invoice line links to more than one sale order line, the cost\n"
"comes from the lowest-database-id line among those that sell the invoice\n"
"line's product. No standard invoicing flow creates that case -- the line\n"
"matcher never offers an invoice line that already carries a sale link --\n"
"so it only arises through a direct write, an import or a server action.\n"
"\n"
"If no linked sale order line sells the invoice line's product -- for\n"
"example after changing the product on a draft invoice line -- the cost\n"
"falls back to the product's, exactly as if the line had no sale source.\n"
"\n"
"The invoice margin percentage is measured against revenue **before** the\n"
"down-payment deduction, so it is not the invoice margin over its own\n"
"untaxed total. On a 1000.00 order invoiced after a 100.00 advance it\n"
"reads 50%, not the 54.76% the net revenue would give.\n"
"\n"
"The \"Show Invoice Margin\" security option hides the margin fields in the\n"
"backend views that ``account_invoice_margin`` defines; this module adds\n"
"no group and no view of its own. It is a view-level control, not a\n"
"model-level one: the fields carry no ``groups=``, so anyone who can read\n"
"the invoice line can read them through RPC, an export or a custom view.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/issues/new?body=module:%20account_invoice_margin_sale%0Aversion:%2019.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
"* Tecnativa\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"-  `AgroMarin <https://www.agromarin.mx>`__:\n"
"\n"
"   -  Luis Marin\n"
"\n"
"-  `Tecnativa <https://www.tecnativa.com>`__:\n"
"\n"
"   -  Sergio Teruel\n"
"   -  Carlos Dauden\n"
"   -  Víctor Martínez\n"
"\n"
"-  `Open Source Integrators <https://www.opensourceintegrators.com>`__:\n"
"\n"
"   -  Bhavesh Odedra\n"
